				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\text{Fractional}}\;{\text{calcium}}\;{\text{absorption}}\;(\% ) = \frac{{{\text{Calcium}}\;{\text{intake}}\;{\text{(g)}} - {\text{fecal}}\;{\text{calcium}}\;{\text{excretion}}\;{\text{(g)}}}}{{{\text{Calcium}}\;{\text{intake}}\;{\text{(g)}}}} \times 100$$\end{document}Fractionalcalciumabsorption(%)=Calciumintake(g)-fecalcalciumexcretion(g)Calciumintake(g)×100where, calcium intake is amount of calcium intake from diet over 3-day balance study, fecal calcium excretion is the amount of calcium presented in feces over 3-day balance study.
